# Sample Data Processing Agreement under the DPDP Act, 2023

A sample Data Processing Agreement (DPA) between an e-commerce company (the **Data Fiduciary**) and a storage and management provider (the **Data Processor**), drafted to follow India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act) and the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025 (DPDP Rules).

> **Disclaimer:** This is a sample template for learning and portfolio purposes. It is not legal advice. All parties, addresses, CINs, contacts and sub-processors are fictional. Have a qualified lawyer review any agreement before using it in practice.

## Why this project

Section 8(2) of the DPDP Act allows a Data Fiduciary to engage a Data Processor only under a valid contract. The Act does not say what that contract must contain, but the Rules (for example Rule 6 on security safeguards) expect processor contracts to carry security obligations. This project turns those requirements into a working agreement, to show how regulatory text becomes contract clauses.

## The scenario

| | |
|---|---|
| **Data Fiduciary** | Thunder E-commerce (fictional), Bengaluru |
| **Data Processor** | Star Technologies Pvt. Ltd. (fictional), Hyderabad |
| **Services** | Storage and management of platform users' personal data |
| **Governing law** | Laws of India; arbitration seated in Bengaluru |

## What the agreement covers

- Appointment, roles and processing only on documented instructions
- Duties of the fiduciary (lawful basis, notice, accuracy) and of the processor
- Security safeguards and a breach notification chain from processor to fiduciary to the Data Protection Board
- Sub-processor approval and flow-down of obligations
- Data location and cross-border transfers
- Retention, erasure and return of data
- Support for Data Principals' rights and grievances
- Audit, confidentiality, liability (capped at 12 months' fees, with carve-outs), term and termination
- Four annexures: description of processing, security measures, approved sub-processors, and contacts

